At Luxury Concept, oud is approached as a composition-dependent ingredient. Its identity is not singular. It shifts depending on what surrounds it in the formula. The same material can feel dry or resinous, dark or luminous, based on its context.

This adaptability is what keeps oud central to modern perfumery. It works across floral, spicy, woody, amber, and fresh compositions without losing presence. It does not define the fragrance alone. Its expression is formed through the surrounding structure.

